## 21. AUTOMATED TESTING

Use the existing test framework and implement actual tests.

### Notification Center tests

- Notification list loads.
- Unread count matches actual records.
- Mark one as read works.
- Mark all as read works.
- Filters and pagination work.
- Dismissal works if implemented.
- Notifications persist after refresh.

### Budget alert tests

- Correct threshold generates an alert.
- Duplicate scheduler runs do not duplicate alerts.
- Alerts use actual budget calculations.
- A new budget period permits the appropriate new alerts.
- Empty or zero-value budgets are handled safely.

### Recurring reminder tests

- Eligible active schedules generate reminders.
- Paused and cancelled schedules do not generate inappropriate reminders.
- Each reminder window is deduplicated.
- Schedule changes update future reminders.
- Timezone and date boundaries are handled correctly.

### Savings goal tests

- Milestone alerts match actual progress.
- Completion alerts are not duplicated.
- Deadline alerts use the real target date.
- Contributions are not counted twice.

### Summary tests

- Weekly and monthly totals match existing calculations.
- Summary periods are correct.
- Empty periods are handled.
- Each summary is generated only once per reporting period.

### Security tests

- Users cannot access another user's notifications.
- Unauthenticated requests are rejected.
- Arbitrary notification creation is blocked.
- Invalid action references are rejected.
- Scheduler endpoints are protected.
- Secrets are not exposed in responses.

### Integration and regression tests

- Generated alerts link to valid pages.
- Existing preferences are respected.
- Dashboard, transactions, budgets, analytics, savings goals, recurring transactions, and reports remain functional.
- Mobile and desktop layouts remain usable.

Run the available automated tests and report their actual outcomes. Do not claim tests passed if they were not executed.

